questions.question:
Consider compounds A, B and C with following structural formulae
A = CH_{3} – CH_{2} – CH_{2} – CH_{2} – OH
B = CH_{2} = CH – CH_{2} – CH_{3}
C = HO – CH_{2} – CH_{2} – CH(OH) – CH_{3}
For the conversion of B from A, reagent (D) required is ______ and structural formula of product (E) obtained when C undergoes same reaction using excess reagent (D) is ______

questions.explanation:
### 1) Ozonolysis of alkene

Ozonolysis of an alkene followed by reductive workup (Zn, H₂O) results in the cleavage of the C=C double bond to form aldehydes and/or ketones. It does not produce alcohols.
\text{>C=C<} \xrightarrow[\text{Zn, H}_2\text{O}]{\text{O}_3} \text{-C(=O)- , -C(=O)-}

### 2) Hydroboration – oxidation of alkene

This reaction converts an alkene into an alcohol. It is a correct method for alcohol preparation.
\text{R}_1\text{R}_2\text{C=CH}_2 \xrightarrow{\text{BH}_3} \text{R}_1-\underset{\text{R}_2}{\underset{|}{\text{C}}}H-\text{CH}_2-\text{BH}_2 \xrightarrow{\text{OH}^-} \text{R}_1-\underset{\text{R}_2}{\underset{|}{\text{C}}}H-\text{CH}_2-\text{OH}

### 3) Reaction of alkyl halide with aqueous NaOH

This is a nucleophilic substitution reaction where an alkyl halide reacts with aqueous NaOH to form an alcohol. It is a correct method.
\text{R-X} + \text{NaOH} \longrightarrow \text{R-OH} + \text{NaX}

### 4) Reaction of Ketone with RMgBr followed by hydrolysis

A ketone reacts with a Grignard reagent (RMgBr) followed by hydrolysis to produce a tertiary alcohol. This is a correct method.
\text{R}_1-\overset{\text{O}}{\overset{||}{\text{C}}}-\text{R}_2 + \text{R'MgX} \longrightarrow \text{R}_1-\underset{\text{OMgX}}{\underset{|}{\overset{\text{R'}}{\overset{|}{\text{C}}}}}-\text{R}_2 \xrightarrow{\text{H}_3\text{O}^+} \text{R}_1-\underset{\text{OH}}{\underset{|}{\overset{\text{R'}}{\overset{|}{\text{C}}}}}-\text{R}_2 + \text{Mg(OH)X}
Since ozonolysis of an alkene yields carbonyl compounds and not alcohols, it is the incorrect method of preparation among the given options.

